foreign  dear colleagues it is an honor for the  European Parliament to have the  president of Slovakia Susanna chaputova  with us here today Madam president  diazuzana welcome  thank you for your vocal promotion of  the values of equality and diversity  that this house and our Europe holds so  dear  last week's double murder at the heart  of Bratislava is a reminder to us  of the constant need to fight back  against hate and defend our lgbtiq  community President chaputava we know  you also as a firm defender of freedom  of speech  soon we will mark five years  since the murder of Slovak journalist  Jan kuchiak and Martina kushnerova that  shocked us to our core this house Madam  president will always remember Jan and  Martina and you will always find us as  an ally in the defense of values  dear Susanna let me quote your words in  a speech that you gave at the United  Nations General Assembly you said that  solidarity should be our binding  principle not an option and your country  Slovakia has demonstrated what  solidarity means by welcoming more than  half a million Ukrainian refugees since  the onset of War by being at the  Forefront of political and military aid  to Ukraine Slovakia has shown time and  again that it can lead thank you for  your country's leadership at this  critical moment for Europe president  chaputova the floor is yours  come on  president  honorable members  the representatives of the Czech  presidency of the council my fellow  Europeans  it's an honor and privilege to be here  and to address the Beating Heart of the  European Union's democracy here in  Strasbourg  this is a city where the modern concept  of Defending Universal human rights  was translated into concrete  institutions  while serving a broader purpose I see  the European Parliament as one of them  my message today is simple  if we don't start defending democracy it  will cease to exist  the date of my speech here was planned  long ago  I couldn't have expected that the recent  homophobic murder of yurai Van college  and matus Horvath on the streets of  Bratislava would remind us of this  simple truth so painfully  it's hard to put in words the grief felt  in Slovakia cities in the past few days  because I hate decided to kill love  just because the killer couldn't not  accept that love can come in different  forms  this was an assault not just on young  people from the lgbtiq community  it was an attack on everyone in Slovakia  because hate crimes always Target the  very essence of what our society stands  for  I would like to assure you that hatred  doesn't dominate our society  I will come that Slovakia Civil Society  immediately and resolutely condemned  this attack  just yesterday the Slovak Parliament  adopted a resolution strongly condemning  these are terrorist attacks and ensuring  all minorities that they are valuable  members of our society  in its Essence democracy is the rule by  the majority in the interest of all with  a key emphasis on the protection of  minorities  if we are failing in their protection we  are undermining democracy itself  in my view the defense of and protection  of democracy is the core mission of our  generation of political leaders  the task ahead of us is to bring Europe  back into balance  which is shaken by crisis from within  and without a balance between our rights  and our commitments  between our security and our prosperity  which we have partly built through  dependence on those who wish to destroy  our democracy  a balance in which we can have different  opinions but where we are bound by the  values of Freedom solidarity and the  liberal democracy  and now please allow me to switch into  Slovak so even here into European  parliament's chamber one can hear the  beautiful Slovak language  president  Madam president honorable members  the balance that I've mentioned  has been threatened in the past two  years by two major crises  the pandemic and the security crisis  caused by Russia by invading Ukraine  as a European Union we reacted the right  way to both crises in the pandemic the  national closing of borders and the race  who would procure more  face masks were quickly replaced by a  common approach and solidarity we  started to recover our economy  post-pandemic with the help of the  resilience and  recovery facility and solidarity is  shared also beyond our borders we are  today one of the biggest Global donors  of vaccines against correlate 19 and  equally decisively have we reacted to  the war that Vladimir Putin waged on the  24th of February against our Eastern  neighbor let us remember that this war  only intensified on this Gloomy February  morning that Russia waged this war long  before first by disinformation and  propaganda and since 2014 also in  military way with the clear goal to  subjugate Ukraine or to destroy it  we have imposed the most extensive  sanctions as the European Union against  Russia  sanctions that have never been this  extensive against any developed economy  we provide political Financial  humanitarian and most of the countries  including Slovakia also military aids to  Ukraine  very important is the European  perspective that we offer to Ukraine and  I'm convinced that one day it will  culminate in a full-fledged membership  without Aid we have one goal to achieve  peace however peace has to be just  otherwise it would only be a temporary  ceasefire  we have  opened not only our homes but also our  hearts to those who had to flee War  some 800 000 people crossed just the  Slovak Ukrainian border and many of  those remained in our country and I'm  very proud of the solidarity and Aid  that was offered by our citizens  both crises left the Europeans  not only with fear and worries but also  with the experience of a very strong  europe-wide empathy and unity and this  experience shows us that the best way to  overcome any challenges that we face as  Union is our Unity cooperation and  solidarity  ladies and gentlemen our efforts to  restore the balance in Europe does not  do not stop here it is paradoxical that  in a situation where we are  unprecedentedly United against external  challenges we also face very strong  internal pressures they are caused by a  Confluence of several crises but also by  ignoring our vulnerabilities for a long  time if we do not cope with these  European crises we run the risk that  they will grow into a crisis of Europe  millions of how European households and  companies are threatened by skyrocketing  Energy prices today these prices began  to rise even before the war since Russia  has already begun to reduce gas supplies  to Europe already last summer and it  started thus to restore distort the  European energy Market  and threaten our citizens Slovakia which  until recently had 85 percent of its gas  from Russia  managed to reduce its dependency to 33  thanks to diversification however we  never know when a Vladimir Putin stops  any gas supplies for good as a union we  have to address the courses and the  impacts of this crisis the right  Solutions therefore have to be European  common and in solidarity those that will  urgently help all in a difficult  situation all member states and apart  from compensations will allow an  agreement on a common gap on gas prices  we need to decouple the prices of  electricity and gas because even today  countries such as Slovakia are  generating most of his electricity from  low carbon sources pay inadequately high  prices for it and therefore I would like  to ask you to support such Solutions  however apart from the consequences we  have to address the causes that brought  us here never again may we remain on one  supplier as a union and never again May  our economic model and prosperity depend  on fossil fuels alone the commitment to  become a climate neutral continent by  2050 can no longer be delayed or put in  question first and foremost we have to  help those  who are hit the hardest by the energy  crisis but the goal is clear we need to  innovate innovate our development model  in order to use renewable energy sources  to a greater extent and destroy our own  Planet less  we must become Global leader not only in  our climate commitments or Ambitions but  also in implementing them  we will only survive if we restore the  balance between our way of life and the  planet where we live  honorable members  today  we Face a crisis of democratic rules and  their respect each country that joined  the European Union and each country that  wishes to join has to be and has to  remain a liberal democracy  being a member of this club is not an  entitlement it's a privilege  it is not enough to achieve membership  in this club the membership has to be  constantly updated with a clear  understanding and respect of common  values values such as the rule of law  division of power  Independence of the Judiciary freedom of  the media or protection of minorities  if these cornerstones on which our  community is built are under attack we  have to have to act to protect them I  want to emphasize that we do not like  the rules as much as we like the  consistency in enforcing them if our  measures are not decisive problems will  grow and those who violate the values of  the European Union will encourage and  Inspire others the very notion of  liberal democracy  is being disinterpreted misunderstood  questioned and attacked by the Extremes  in many of our countries even though  there is not a single model of liberal  democracy I am certain that illiberal  illiberal democracy are two incompatible  Notions  honorable members our Democratic rules  are today abused to destroy democracy  itself  freedom of speech is one of the most  important Democratic rights we need to  protect it but it's not without  limitations  how could it happen that we let freedom  of speech escalate to verbal crimes  how could we elevate it many times to an  absolute right this is not Democratic  this is stupid the freedom of speech  cannot be a cover to spread intolerance  lies and disinformation  nowhere is this problem more acute than  in social networks the radicalized  teenager that killed two young men last  week and injured a third-person  industries of Bratislava was greatly  inspired on social media and before the  murder he published a long pamphlet on  Social Network full of hatred against  various minorities  this murder did happen in Slovakia but  the risk of such crimes concerns all of  us  we witness  a growing aggression against minorities  and the growing right-wing extremism in  many parts of Europe  the worsening of the socioeconomic  situation only enhances the in  confidence of radicals we need to be  aware that any attack based on hatred is  an attack against the very values of the  European Union and that include equality  tolerance and respect of Human Rights  it seems that we take a similarly naive  approach to Social Network as we take to  other technological innovations without  due caution we use the benefits without  knowledge and vigilance of their  potential and obvious negative  consequences we use social networks  without being fully aware as a society  how their algorithms May harm us how  they deepen the polarization and enhance  filter bubbles  to believe the truth to live the truth  and to defend the truth is the motto of  one of the founders of the modern Slovak  Nation General Milan rastislav stefanik  in public space it has to apply even  when it seems that it would be more  efficient to shout loudly regardless of  the quality of truthfulness of the  statement instead of listening to each  other engaging in dialogue and caring  for facts let us not let democracy  perish on the naivety of Democrats on  the naive belief that Democratic rights  and freedoms will only be used and never  abused let us not forget that every  right is at the same time an expression  of responsibility and vice versa  and if we do not protect democracy it  may happen that we will be the last  generation to experience it its  protection is the main task of our  generation of political leaders  therefore we have to take appropriate  steps in this area at National level it  is good that the European Parliament  adopted the Digital Services act and I  also welcome the European democracy  action plan what is illegal offline has  to be illegal online  [Applause]  however we need to also do more at the  global level the business model of  social platforms is based on the use of  the lowest human emotions and impulses  social platforms are not just operators  of the proverbial information pipelines  because their profit is directly  proportional to how much hatred how much  aggression lies and this information  flows through these Pipelines  they must therefore bear reasonable  responsibility for the content that is  published on them  Madam president honorable members  the challenges I'm talking about today  make the European Union more fragile  than we may realize and admit the  economic security and energy crisis the  ongoing fragmentation of our societies  and the pressure of illegal migration  these are all bring grounds for  extremism in many member countries of  the Union One election cycle is enough  today and in the Parliamentary benches  even here in this house  in your seats there can be a majority  that does not want to build Europe but  destroy it  therefore may we must not be naive we  must not be lacks and defensive but in  the contrary we must be persistent  courageous and self-confident in the  defense of our common values despite the  inevitability of solving many crises and  perhaps precisely because of it we must  not forget that the performance of  Politics as such should be based on very  clear values that is on the value  um that we have to defend as politician  politicians if we believe and stay true  to these principles this will not be a  show of weakness but the contrary the  first president of Czechoslovakia Thomas  garigma sarek already said 100 years ago  that democracy is not only a political  system but first and foremost is a moral  system let's all think about it when  carrying out our mandate which is a  responsibility and an obligation towards  our citizens if we perceive democracy in  this sense I am sure that we will manage  the crisis we are facing today and thus  fulfill our mission to be the Guardians  and Protectors of democracy of European  values and of the balance thank you  [Applause]  [Applause]  we're finished  thank you very much that concludes  the formal  sitting  and we're there by resume  I was sitting with the votes  I will give one  minute for you to  find your seats and place your voting  cards

